{"title":"2023 AIME II Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Diagram\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Diagram</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_Piboy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by Piboy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic(#3_and_#4)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by The Power of Logic(#3 and #4)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> be an isosceles triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/f/e4fa7992e2858bc742b641de6b3180c038338dcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A = 90^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" /> There exists a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> inside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bc18cfa396469104814028696c42e72aa37242.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PAB = \\angle PBC = \\angle PCA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"217\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/3/9c3c9de3a958b5f6202fc54a236e09e56712a73c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP = 10.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"14\" /> Find the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919b9f77a6985e760286799909be5bfe0152f40e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Diagram\">Diagram</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Diagram\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/c/9ccb1b32a435d0a454f39f5c406ef35b1b7d82f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Made by MRENTHUSIASM */  size(200); pair A, B, C, P;  A = origin; B = (0,10*sqrt(5)); C = (10*sqrt(5),0); P = intersectionpoints(Circle(A,10),Circle(C,20))[0];  dot(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,1.5*SW,linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,1.5*NW,linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,1.5*SE,linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$P$&quot;,P,1.5*NE,linewidth(4));  markscalefactor=0.125; draw(rightanglemark(B,A,C,10),red); draw(anglemark(P,A,B,25),red); draw(anglemark(P,B,C,25),red); draw(anglemark(P,C,A,25),red); add(pathticks(anglemark(P,A,B,25), n = 1, r = 0.1, s = 10, red)); add(pathticks(anglemark(P,B,C,25), n = 1, r = 0.1, s = 10, red)); add(pathticks(anglemark(P,C,A,25), n = 1, r = 0.1, s = 10, red));  draw(A--B--C--cycle^^P--A^^P--B^^P--C); label(&quot;$10$&quot;,midpoint(A--P),dir(-30),blue); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"332\" />\n~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This solution refers to the <b>Diagram</b> section.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/8/0c8a58ff463904c8fefc1dbed830ea7c214a4064.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PAB = \\angle PBC = \\angle PCA = \\theta,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"255\" height=\"18\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/a/9ea87398e22107b505e5766be5bc26f0825f816f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PAC = 90^\\circ-\\theta,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/c/15c53375dc5db4ce4ac5cc2ab0e230ffab1f83a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APC = 90^\\circ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Moreover, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/1/2f1f6c19faa8a9d8fdf5515e524f26ca28a1b681.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PBA = \\angle PCB = 45^\\circ-\\theta,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"224\" height=\"18\" /> as shown below:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/e/8fe6f00cc00a7edc0c03ca1dd350098457935664.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Made by MRENTHUSIASM */  size(250); pair A, B, C, P;  A = origin; B = (0,10*sqrt(5)); C = (10*sqrt(5),0); P = intersectionpoints(Circle(A,10),Circle(C,20))[0];  dot(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,1.5*SW,linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,1.5*NW,linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,1.5*SE,linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$P$&quot;,P,1.5*NE,linewidth(4));  markscalefactor=0.125; draw(rightanglemark(B,A,C,10),red); draw(rightanglemark(A,P,C,10),red); draw(anglemark(P,A,B,25),red); draw(anglemark(P,B,C,25),red); draw(anglemark(P,C,A,25),red); draw(anglemark(A,B,P,25),green); draw(anglemark(B,C,P,25),green); draw(anglemark(C,A,P,25),green); add(pathticks(anglemark(P,A,B,25), n = 1, r = 0.1, s = 10, red)); add(pathticks(anglemark(P,B,C,25), n = 1, r = 0.1, s = 10, red)); add(pathticks(anglemark(P,C,A,25), n = 1, r = 0.1, s = 10, red));  draw(A--B--C--cycle^^P--A^^P--B^^P--C); label(&quot;$10$&quot;,midpoint(A--P),dir(-30),blue); label(&quot;$\\theta$&quot;,A,9.5*dir(76),red); label(&quot;$\\theta$&quot;,C,9.5*dir(168),red); label(&quot;$\\theta$&quot;,B,9*dir(305),red); label(&quot;$45^\\circ-\\theta$&quot;,B,6*dir(235),green); label(&quot;$45^\\circ-\\theta$&quot;,C,6*dir(85),green); label(&quot;$90^\\circ-\\theta$&quot;,A,2*dir(-40),green); [/asy]\" width=\"418\" height=\"352\" />\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/5/975635a50c907157b21dfdb950bc8515bd4435a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PAB \\sim \\triangle PBC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" /> by AA Similarity. The ratio of similitude is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/d/04d5359134587fdca0e150260422a44ffdbec597.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{PA}{PB} = \\frac{PB}{PC} = \\frac{AB}{BC},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"154\" height=\"39\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/9/e991ca8e88d83c2bb2a28f755148f96b451f9bf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{10}{PB} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"87\" height=\"43\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ea2685cce2d1bb271c63d37a7c133222c13b6bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB=10\\sqrt2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"21\" /> Similarly, we can figure out that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/e/fde6cfcf4c82fdd64a5717d813f11cdac1ba7e2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PC=20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Finally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/a/75ac2b056a256ab336fe4b28643adca4015f8ec5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=\\sqrt{10^2+20^2}=10\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"209\" height=\"21\" />, so the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/7/2f7c913410acaba3f027610a619170646b850cf2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac12\\cdot AB\\cdot AC = \\frac12\\cdot (10\\sqrt{5})^2 = \\boxed{250}.\\]\" width=\"274\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>~s214425\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the triangle is a right isosceles triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/0/090841ebac0d7bcee4495a2a7e8404d6c3fc7938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B = \\angle C = 45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Let the common angle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4dbc809f7ba3e3061a79ddab739feef6e5d624aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PAC = 90^\\circ-\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"138\" height=\"16\" />, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/7/427519629b623291ae028a36c5b7c3eaa1d3b227.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APC = 90^\\circ$\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" />. From there, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/6/4068fe73aa58d5b9d8d242968870e67f958ff317.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = \\frac{10}{\\sin\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"92\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/3/de316a6a2bdc5b975aa5c06de6e29f1d24a6195d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABP = 45^\\circ-\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"16\" />, so from law of sines we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c0420bcfdc1d197359f37dd86824bfa3325257e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{10}{\\sin\\theta \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}}=\\frac{10}{\\sin(45^\\circ-\\theta)}.\\]\" width=\"196\" height=\"46\" />\nDividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and multiplying across yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/5/fc5e8f5d77d7987a2a5c868efffe0e3106eb42f2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{2}\\sin(45^\\circ-\\theta)=\\sin\\theta.\\]\" width=\"182\" height=\"21\" />\nFrom here use the sine subtraction formula, and solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/c/4cc6cd401ab7d1f6f198d8b36a1e53d6403555e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\theta$\" width=\"34\" height=\"13\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e278e9f1387f77029fef327b1283f12f6669663.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\cos\\theta-\\sin\\theta&amp;=\\sin\\theta \\\\ 2\\sin\\theta&amp;=\\cos\\theta \\\\ 4\\sin^2\\theta&amp;=\\cos^2\\theta \\\\ 4\\sin^2\\theta&amp;=1-\\sin^2\\theta \\\\ 5\\sin^2\\theta&amp;=1 \\\\ \\sin\\theta&amp;=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"189\" height=\"175\" />\nSubstitute this to find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/0/630ae08f6dcde565aa9569ba2cce818eb519c5fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=10\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"21\" />, thus the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/4/624372b8a8907014fc3901f60cf32e4f6a5ad67e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(10\\sqrt{5})^2}{2}=\\boxed{250}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"133\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>~SAHANWIJETUNGA\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the triangle is a right isosceles triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/0/090841ebac0d7bcee4495a2a7e8404d6c3fc7938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B = \\angle C = 45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Do some angle chasing yielding:\n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/b/e4bbd5d92da01cd1c095144713595522c5a0f0be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APB = \\angle BPC = 135^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"197\" height=\"15\" /></li></ul>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/4/3c4cd6f16617774fe4bae32221a9c7d8a6f7b33b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APC=90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" /></li></ul>\n<p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/a/2bafacfcc1692b03c314685fc143c1899b5956de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=\\frac{10}{\\sin\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"92\" height=\"38\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/5/14589098013cf51bd13b7d32a5476db3ee28f0cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle APC$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is a right triangle. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8adb649f063149ebc97d3ee58c4fd38d4c440846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8adb649f063149ebc97d3ee58c4fd38d4c440846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22ec0d2e4202839322d26a23dcb13f79821df5d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/7/347b3fd7367e4fda2edcf8e082f60caf21a3804f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=\\frac{10}{\\sin\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/b/3abb51c1083918ceed4a721cd0cda31029914d5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=\\frac{10\\sqrt{2}}{\\sin\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"101\" height=\"43\" />. \n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/8/dc89ebf8d3b78eaf5d7f590a250279c37e40fd39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle APB \\sim \\triangle BPC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" /> by a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4dc1409208ff6a3039f4871d85c16763334983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"21\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/9/6d93a3a44e9d23c2ca281b143e4443f41eabe2d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP = 10\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"21\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/e/97e2d89e280699bc449546aec13ea1e05df48cac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PC = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>From Pythagorean theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/0/630ae08f6dcde565aa9569ba2cce818eb519c5fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=10\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"21\" /> so the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/4/624372b8a8907014fc3901f60cf32e4f6a5ad67e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(10\\sqrt{5})^2}{2}=\\boxed{250}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"133\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>~SAHANWIJETUNGA\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the triangle is a right isosceles triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/0/090841ebac0d7bcee4495a2a7e8404d6c3fc7938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B = \\angle C = 45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Notice that in triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e0830febe7535fbbdf19782a978c79c0c9e6cd70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PBC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/e/3cec8bf8e2c0dc3d3acd055fc1b2d8084bea56a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PBC + 45-\\angle PCA = 45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"226\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/7/55725fdddb3bd514eac85bea412b986027c1833d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BPC = 135^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"117\" height=\"15\" />. Similar logic shows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/7/907454db12c49cefdba8eb821c80b8bd1f086a77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APC = 135^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/8/dc89ebf8d3b78eaf5d7f590a250279c37e40fd39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle APB \\sim \\triangle BPC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" /> with ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/a/5fa13cf52d77b955ea83d48c7a23fd87d7f2c89c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1:\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" /> (as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8adb649f063149ebc97d3ee58c4fd38d4c440846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8adb649f063149ebc97d3ee58c4fd38d4c440846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22ec0d2e4202839322d26a23dcb13f79821df5d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> triangle). Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/8/d68d73c051b71ad9f883e686de8eca9bdd10c87d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{PB}=10\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"21\" />. We use the Law of Cosines to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/7/367d4a9f910926d0c0b4d7df5cc453fd3a3045d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} AB^2&amp;=BP^2+AP^2-2ab\\cos(APB) \\\\ &amp;=100+200-2(10)(10\\sqrt{2}\\cos(135^\\circ)) \\\\ &amp;=300+200\\cdot\\sqrt{2}\\cdot\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ &amp;=500. \\end{align*}\" width=\"331\" height=\"119\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is a right triangle, the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/0/e3016764ce5bc6a5b08b4eaf69e89f3d011c4279.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AB^2}{2}=\\frac{500}{2}=\\boxed{250}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"160\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>~Kiran\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/5/a9518ed103cb6898857664595f950f87beba0328.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[X].$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"33\" height=\"20\" /> As in previous solutions, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d25ed70269978bb1e1a24d0078dff791c5775b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APC = 90 ^\\circ, \\triangle BPC \\sim \\triangle APB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"257\" height=\"18\" /> with ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efb8c7e7fd66d3c883c1a520f887a86fc69e4d56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = \\sqrt{2}\\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"21\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/f/76f2f8668ec31d61c90674dc7d7d798349235c5a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {PC}{PB} = \\frac {PB}{PA} = k \\implies PC = k^2 \\cdot AP = 20 \\implies [APC] = \\frac {AP \\cdot PC}{2} = 100.\\]\" width=\"571\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/9/be939ccc9fabf6d409b62e77c99c5c24f79b2382.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[BPC] = k^2 [APB] = 2 [APB].\\]\" width=\"235\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/5/38596ac466b1095a3a09dbff3ed6b41e989b12ff.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB = BC, \\angle PCA = \\angle PAB \\implies \\frac {[APC]}{[APB]} = \\frac {PC}{PA} = 2 \\implies\\]\" width=\"457\" height=\"43\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/0/f90ea4866ba65aafe7f75e8e745be22a7485d7a8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[ABC] = [APB] + [APC] + [BPC] = [APC] \\cdot (\\frac {1}{2} + 1 + 2 \\cdot \\frac {1}{2}) = \\frac {5}{2} \\cdot  [APC] = \\boxed{250}.\\]\" width=\"595\" height=\"38\" />\n<b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2fbd3568caa993c3e20b1ff5616e34d664fc65b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PCA = \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />. Then, by trig Ceva's: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/c/c9cafce60a2d5bc9734bc20a326437f60266333a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{\\sin^3(\\theta)}{\\sin(90-\\theta) \\cdot \\left(\\sin(45-\\theta)\\right)^2} &amp;= 1 \\\\ \\sin^3(\\theta) &amp;= \\cos(\\theta) \\cdot \\left(\\sin(45) \\cos(\\theta) - \\cos(45) \\sin(\\theta)\\right)^2 \\\\ 2\\sin^3(\\theta) &amp;= \\cos(\\theta) \\cdot \\left(\\cos(\\theta) - \\sin(\\theta)\\right)^2 \\\\ 2\\sin^2(\\theta) &amp;= \\cot(\\theta) \\cdot \\left(1 - 2\\sin(\\theta)\\cos(\\theta)\\right) \\\\ 2\\sin^2(\\theta) &amp;= \\cot(\\theta) - 2\\cos^2(\\theta) \\\\ \\cot(\\theta) &amp;= 2 \\\\ \\sin(\\theta) &amp;= \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"546\" height=\"236\" />\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/c/05c30f7f918e06a4bd4c6782e24c66bf0d11b0b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APC$\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" /> is a right angle. Therefore: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/e/66e0ac561c9b7ab7fce7e9ae951aca627056e9ae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sin(\\theta) &amp;= \\frac{AP}{AC} \\\\ AC &amp;= \\frac{10}{\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}} \\\\ &amp;= 10\\sqrt{5} \\\\ |ABC| &amp;= \\frac{AC^2}{2} \\\\ &amp;= \\boxed{250}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"118\" height=\"195\" />\n~ConcaveTriangle\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is one of the two Brocard Points of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. (The angle equalities given in the problem are equivalent to the definition of a Brocard point.) By the Brocard point formula,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/4/cf45abbae0ed20daa9b626a8c37dfce01e6f5c13.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\cot(\\phi) = \\cot(A)+\\cot(B)+\\cot(C)  \\end{align*}\" width=\"273\" height=\"18\" />\n, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/1/2c175f60eecef1de7560c3bdea495d69f26f719d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/4/f64cd0f9104ed8209114f939ba5fe63a529a7e28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PAB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />.(This is also called the Brocard angle of triangle ABC). Because the triangle is an isosceles right triangle, the cotangents are easy to compute:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/7/947fd7ea0b32bfb0b26b413af4a5c012050a8312.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\cot(\\phi) = 0 + 1 + 1 \\\\ \\cot(\\phi) = 2\\end{align*}\" width=\"144\" height=\"43\" />\nBy definition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/c/a1caee4f145b4e773156f8a106db756494082a7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot(\\phi) = \\frac{\\cos(\\phi)}{\\sin(\\phi)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"129\" height=\"45\" />. By the Pythagorean identity, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/4/454cc15f33f6e85c0b3acc9f97396504d759e9a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\phi)=\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"113\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/b/d4bf5ef3f0d078895206d9ffada65edc7ef1089b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\phi) = \\cos(\\phi)=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"175\" height=\"43\" />. Consider triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/b/92b38136cabb69ee2f7b5711190e0042354f3419.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APB$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. By the problem condition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/1/6816e1a9117457e58bc81adeb9d60b318da5d678.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PBA = 45-\\phi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37ee35d5a796ac18cb5369fc3cb60ae228f3bb84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BPA = 135^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/4/69458c97b2fbcac4f0582072c3163dd9312a473a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\sin{45-\\theta} = \\sin{45}\\cos{\\phi}-\\cos{45}\\sin{\\phi} = \\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}\\end{align*}\" width=\"350\" height=\"41\" />\nNow, we can use the Law of Sines.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e18c3cdc1d4547ceaf57e5e1ac201346300e44d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{AP}{\\sin{45-\\theta}}&amp;=\\frac{AB}{\\sin{135}} \\\\ 10 \\sqrt{10} &amp;= \\sqrt{2} AB \\\\ AB &amp;= 10 \\sqrt{5} \\end{align*}\" width=\"156\" height=\"95\" />\nTherefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/9/4198384801e35778d76d49359182312969b73de9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[ABC] = \\frac{1}{2} (AB)^2 = \\boxed{250}.\\]\" width=\"204\" height=\"37\" />\n~ewei12\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8\">Solution 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/3/59346d02fd6e00874971e2e01a511d66d7b54535.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APC = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/e/37ee35d5a796ac18cb5369fc3cb60ae228f3bb84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BPA = 135^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/a/aba9118e643b00da296a3ba80bc21da92244dfb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CPB = 135^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"117\" height=\"15\" /> (from Solution 4). Now let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/9/b5969c2cfb1ffadf981fbbddcf796c8eb0037546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 0$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/8/4980e25a031b1df48d2e5fbeb313e29190bec158.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 10i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" />. Then by the angle restrictions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/8/e48e9c3297514d304243ef5ed4fcd17b39fb6a88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = m + 10i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/4/914e07fb6b9c5a0ac917c28d3a1149b868b717db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = -n + (n+10)i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"153\" height=\"20\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/5/6851ca945f78b10a85c14fc57fbaf75e69f57241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"11\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/2/45274538eee6ed6129c877cb1be2582488d700ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/5/805771080a8067e502dbeaac77195b7dd27ea4cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ci = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f1bc23abefb0bb711e141d1fd2daf9521657d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m + 10i)i = -n + (n+10)i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"228\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/1/fa17013a449147f7545eaf8c6efd44b5b9fa2034.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/a/4aa8e9bfd71420bc023bff80f4e1c45ec19b4f5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = \\sqrt{10^2 + 20^2} = \\sqrt{500}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"210\" height=\"21\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/2/4924d7be0619b94eb165988378c62241d6a9d486.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC] = \\frac{1}{2} AB^2 = \\boxed{250}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~aliz\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=APSUN-9Z_AU\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=APSUN-9Z_AU</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_Piboy\">Video Solution 2 by Piboy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by Piboy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-WUhMmdXCxU&amp;t=26s&amp;ab_channel=Piboy\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-WUhMmdXCxU&amp;t=26s&amp;ab_channel=Piboy</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic.28.233_and_.234.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic(#3_and_#4)\">Video Solution by The Power of Logic(#3 and #4)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by The Power of Logic(#3 and #4)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/dS9K1o4gCA0\">https://youtu.be/dS9K1o4gCA0</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II\" title=\"2023 AIME II\">2023 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2023 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2023 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2023\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2023 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2023 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2023 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2023 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AIME_II_Problems/Proble